{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Layout & Responsiveness
    
    Use a responsive CSS Grid layout.
    
    Allow merchants to control rows and columns separately for:
    
    Desktop
    
    Tablet
    
    Mobile
    
    Grid should automatically adapt and reflow based on device settings.
    
    Adjustable grid spacing (gap).
    
    Optimized, lightweight, and mobile-first.
    
    Heading
    
    Large centered heading text: “Projects”
    
    Heading slightly overlaps the grid (hero-style overlay).
    
    Controls in theme editor:
    
    Font size
    
    Opacity
    
    Vertical offset
    
    Heading must remain responsive across all devices.
    
    Image Management (MAX 24 IMAGES)
    
    Provide two selectable image modes using a toggle:
    
    Mode 1: Individual Image Blocks
    
    Merchant can add images one by one.
    
    Each image block includes:
    
    Image picker
    
    Optional link URL
    
    Optional alt text
    
    Mode 2: Bulk Gallery Upload
    
    Allow merchant to select up to 24 images at once.
    
    Images must come from Shopify Files (store uploads) — NOT products.
    
    Automatically place one image per grid cell.
    
    No manual block setup required.
    
    Images must render correctly immediately.
    
    Image Display Rules
    
    Enforce a consistent aspect ratio.
    
    Use object-fit: cover.
    
    Automatically crop images to fill grid cells.
    
    Rounded corners with adjustable radius (default ~24px).
    
    Fix any issues where images fail to display.
    
    Hover & Animation
    
    Hover effect:
    
    Subtle zoom-in
    
    Soft shadow fade-in
    
    Optional morphing animation:
    
    Images smoothly transition into the next image within the same grid cell.
    
    Crossfade or scale-morph effect.
    
    Adjustable animation speed.
    
    Animation toggle on/off.
    
    Use CSS-based animations only (no heavy JavaScript).
    
    Styling Controls
    
    Add theme settings for:
    
    Background color
    
    Section padding (top & bottom)
    
    Grid spacing
    
    Image corner radius
    
    Animation toggle and speed
    
    Technical Requirements
    
    Shopify Online Store 2.0 JSON section structure
    
    Semantic HTML
    
    Responsive CSS
    
    No external libraries
    
    Performance-optimized
    
    Clean and well-labeled schema
    
    End Goal
    
    The section should allow merchants to:
    
    Upload up to 24 images easily
    
    Choose bet, we added the images but the images arent showing, Rows + Columns Controls (per device)
    
    Add theme editor controls so the merchant can set columns and rows separately for Desktop / Tablet / Mobile.
    
    Example settings: desktop_columns, desktop_rows, tablet_columns, tablet_rows, mobile_columns, mobile_rows.
    
    The grid must render exactly rows × columns visible cells per device (up to the 24 image max) and reflow correctly on breakpoint changes.
    
    Keep adjustable grid gap setting.
    
    Morphing Rotation (always ON)
    
    Remove the animation toggle. The morphing/crossfade rotation must always be enabled.
    
    Every grid cell should automatically switch to a different image every 3 seconds.
    
    Use CSS-based transitions for the morph/crossfade/scale effect (no heavy JS; only minimal logic to swap image sources).
    
    No Duplicates On Screen
    
    At any moment, the same image must not appear in more than one grid cell.
    
    When rotating, ensure the newly selected image is not currently visible in any other cell.
    
    If there aren’t enough unique images to fill the grid (e.g., fewer images than cells), gracefully handle it (e.g., reduce filled cells or pause rotation) but never show duplicates simultaneously.
    
    Keep Existing Requirements
    
    Maintain current heading overlap controls (font size, opacity, vertical offset) and responsiveness.
    
    Maintain consistent aspect ratio, object-fit: cover, rounded corners with radius setting, and hover zoom + soft shadow.
    
